max-command-size: MAX_COMMAND_SIZE = MAX_RESPONSE_SIZE = 4096 - 0x80

Classification: profile setting.

The maximum command and response sizes are a profile choice; version 185
raises them to 8192 octets for post-quantum algorithms (which the profile
disables), tpm-rs (like the public mstpm20 profile) uses 4096 - 0x80, which
determines which commands are rejected with TPM_RC_COMMAND_SIZE and the
reported TPM_PT_MAX_COMMAND_SIZE/TPM_PT_MAX_RESPONSE_SIZE.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Common.h b/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Common.h
--- a/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Common.h
+++ b/TPMCmd/TpmConfiguration/TpmConfiguration/TpmProfile_Common.h
@@ -218,8 +218,8 @@
 // offset 0x80, so the net size available is:
 // PQC will overrun these sizes, so systems targeting PC CRB
 // need to use the new chunked CRB interface in PC Client PTP 1.07+
-#define  MAX_COMMAND_SIZE               (8192)
-#define  MAX_RESPONSE_SIZE              (8192)
+#define  MAX_COMMAND_SIZE               (4096-0x80)
+#define  MAX_RESPONSE_SIZE              (4096-0x80)
